      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:2:1:100:1",
      "text": [
        " سَمِعْتُ أَبَا عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) يَقُولُ الْمُؤْمِنَةُ أَعَزُّ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِ وَ الْمُؤْمِنُ أَعَزُّ مِنَ الْكِبْرِيتِ الْأَحْمَرِ فَمَنْ رَأَى مِنْكُمُ الْكِبْرِيتَ الْأَحْمَرَ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad Bin Isa, from Muhammad Bin Sinan, from Quteyba Al A’ash who said, ",
          "‘I heard Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> saying: ‘The <span class=\"iTxt\">Momina</span> (female Believer) is more cherished than the <span class=\"iTxt\">Momin</span>, and the <span class=\"iTxt\">Momin</span> is more cherished than the alchemy. So who from you has (ever) seen alchemy?’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "1. Muhammad ibn Yahya has narrated from Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn ‘Isa from Muhammad ibn Sinan from Qutaybah al-‘A’sha’ who has said the following: “I heard abu ‘Abd Allah (a.s.) saying, ‘The female believer is more valued than a male believer and a male believer is more valued than alchemy. Who among you has ever seen alchemy?’” "
        ]
      }
